$ python3 tmp/R69/replay/llvm/utils/lit/lit.py --help
usage: lit [-h] [--version] [-j N] [--config-prefix NAME] [-D NAME=VAL]
           [--test-output {off,failed,all}]
           [--print-result-after {off,failed,all}]
           [--diagnostic-level {error,warning,note}] [--terse-summary]
           [--no-terse-summary] [-q] [-s] [-v] [-vv] [-a] [-r] [-o PATH]
           [--progress-bar] [--no-progress-bar] [--show-excluded]
           [--show-skipped] [--show-unsupported] [--show-pass]
           [--show-flakypass] [--show-xfail] [--gtest-sharding]
           [--no-gtest-sharding] [--path PATH] [--vg] [--vg-leak]
           [--vg-arg ARG] [--no-execute] [--xunit-xml-output XUNIT_XML_OUTPUT]
           [--report-failures-only] [--resultdb-output RESULTDB_OUTPUT]
           [--time-trace-output TIME_TRACE_OUTPUT]
           [--timeout MAXINDIVIDUALTESTTIME] [--max-retries-per-test N]
           [--max-failures MAX_FAILURES] [--allow-empty-runs]
           [--per-test-coverage] [--ignore-fail] [--update-tests]
           [--skip-test-time-recording | --time-tests] [--max-tests N]
           [--max-time N] [--order {lexical,random,smart}] [--shuffle] [-i]
           [--filter REGEX] [--filter-out REGEX] [--filter-failed]
           [--xfail LIST] [--xfail-not LIST] [--exclude-xfail]
           [--num-shards M] [--run-shard N] [--debug] [--show-suites]
           [--show-tests] [--show-used-features]
           TEST_PATH [TEST_PATH ...]

positional arguments:
  TEST_PATH             File or path to include in the test suite

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --version             show program's version number and exit
  -j N, --threads N, --workers N
                        Number of workers used for testing
  --config-prefix NAME  Prefix for 'lit' config files
  -D NAME=VAL, --param NAME=VAL
                        Add 'NAME' = 'VAL' to the user defined parameters

Output Format:
  --test-output {off,failed,all}
                        Control whether the executed commands and their
                        outputs are printed after each test has executed
                        (default off). If --print-result-after is set lower
                        than the level given to --test-output, --print-result-
                        after is raised to match.
  --print-result-after {off,failed,all}
                        Control which the executed test names and results are
                        printed after each test has executed (default all). If
                        --test-output is set higher than the level given to
                        --print-result-after, --test-output is lowered to
                        match.
  --diagnostic-level {error,warning,note}
                        Control how verbose lit diagnostics should be (default
                        note)
  --terse-summary       Print the elapsed time and the number of passed tests
                        after all tests have finished (default on)
  --no-terse-summary    Don't show the elapsed time after all tests have
                        finished, and only show the number of failed tests.
  -q, --quiet           Alias for '--diagnostic-level=error --test-output=off
                        --terse-summary'
  -s, --succinct        Alias for '--progress-bar --print-result-after=failed'
  -v, --verbose         For failed tests, show all output. For example, each
                        command is printed before it is executed, so the last
                        printed command is the one that failed. Alias for '--
                        test-output=failed'
  -vv, --echo-all-commands
                        Deprecated alias for -v.
  -a, --show-all        Enable -v, but for all tests not just failed tests.
                        Alias for '--test-output=all'
  -r, --relative-paths  Print paths relative to CWD
  -o PATH, --output PATH
                        Write test results to the provided path
  --progress-bar        Show curses based progress bar
  --no-progress-bar     Do not use curses based progress bar (default)
  --show-excluded       Show excluded tests (EXCLUDED)
  --show-skipped        Show skipped tests (SKIPPED)
  --show-unsupported    Show unsupported tests (UNSUPPORTED)
  --show-pass           Show passed tests (PASS)
  --show-flakypass      Show passed with retry tests (FLAKYPASS)
  --show-xfail          Show expectedly failed tests (XFAIL)

Test Execution:
  --gtest-sharding      Enable sharding for GoogleTest format
  --no-gtest-sharding   Disable sharding for GoogleTest format
  --path PATH           Additional paths to add to testing environment
  --vg                  Run tests under valgrind
  --vg-leak             Check for memory leaks under valgrind
  --vg-arg ARG          Specify an extra argument for valgrind
  --no-execute          Don't execute any tests (assume PASS)
  --xunit-xml-output XUNIT_XML_OUTPUT
                        Write XUnit-compatible XML test reports to the
                        specified file
  --report-failures-only
                        Only include unresolved, timed out, failed and
                        unexpectedly passed tests in the report
  --resultdb-output RESULTDB_OUTPUT
                        Write LuCI ResultDB compatible JSON to the specified
                        file
  --time-trace-output TIME_TRACE_OUTPUT
                        Write Chrome tracing compatible JSON to the specified
                        file
  --timeout MAXINDIVIDUALTESTTIME
                        Maximum time to spend running a single test (in
                        seconds). 0 means no time limit. [Default: 0]
  --max-retries-per-test N
                        Maximum number of allowed retry attempts per test
                        (NOTE: The config.test_retry_attempts test suite
                        option and ALLOWED_RETRIES keyword always take
                        precedence)
  --max-failures MAX_FAILURES
                        Stop execution after the given number of failures.
  --allow-empty-runs    Do not fail the run if all tests are filtered out
  --per-test-coverage   Enable individual test case coverage
  --ignore-fail         Exit with status zero even if some tests fail
  --update-tests        Try to update regression tests to reflect current
                        behavior, if possible
  --skip-test-time-recording
                        Do not track elapsed wall time for each test
  --time-tests          Track elapsed wall time for each test printed in a
                        histogram

Test Selection:
  --max-tests N         Maximum number of tests to run
  --max-time N          Maximum time to spend testing (in seconds)
  --order {lexical,random,smart}
                        Test order to use (default: smart)
  --shuffle             Run tests in random order (DEPRECATED: use
                        --order=random)
  -i, --incremental     Run failed tests first (DEPRECATED: use --order=smart)
  --filter REGEX        Only run tests with paths matching the given regular
                        expression
  --filter-out REGEX    Filter out tests with paths matching the given regular
                        expression
  --filter-failed       Only run tests which failed in the previous run
  --xfail LIST          XFAIL tests with paths in the semicolon separated list
  --xfail-not LIST      do not XFAIL tests with paths in the semicolon
                        separated list
  --exclude-xfail       exclude XFAIL tests (unless they are in the --xfail-
                        not list). Note: This option is implemented in
                        lit.TestRunner.parseIntegratedTestScript and so will
                        have no effect on test formats that do not call that
                        and do not implement the option separately.
  --num-shards M        Split testsuite into M pieces and only run one
  --run-shard N         Run shard #N of the testsuite

Debug and Experimental Options:
  --debug               Enable debugging (for 'lit' development)
  --show-suites         Show discovered test suites and exit
  --show-tests          Show all discovered tests and exit
  --show-used-features  Show all features used in the test suite (in XFAIL,
                        UNSUPPORTED and REQUIRES) and exit
exit_code=0
wrapper_exit_code=0
